  "id": "recipient-pin.behavior.canonical",
  "kind": "recipient-pin.behavior",
  "milestone": "M6",
  "title": "Recipient comparison is eip155 lowercase-hex and solana verbatim base58 (SPEC §6.4)",
  "spec": ["SPEC §6", "SPEC §6.4", "SPEC §3.4", "ADR-028"],
  "description": "The pin comparison is canonical per network family (SPEC §6.4), core-path with no chain libraries. On eip155, a pin administered in mixed-case hex admits a reserve presenting the same address in a DIFFERENT case — both sides lowercase before comparison (the sameAddress rule; no EIP-55 checksum). The pin readback preserves the verbatim administered string. On solana, base58 is injective and case-sensitive, so a pin admits an exact-match reserve and refuses one that differs only in case — a lowercased base58 is a different key and is not-allowlisted.",
